Count All ((i,j) pairs such that b[i] - b[j] == k (count of such pairs.) [i<j] 

Explanation:

In this we need to find the number of pairs such that the ABSOLUTE difference between 2 numbers ==k.
So we are going to check if for a number, the num+k exists in the hashmap and the num-k exists in the hasmap.
if they exists we add it to the count.
and then we add the current num to map by updating it.

Code:
class Solution {
    public int countKDifference(int[] nums, int k) {
        HashMap<Integer,Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
        int count=0;

        for(int num: nums){
            count+=map.getOrDefault(num-k,0);
            count+=map.getOrDefault(num+k,0);

            map.put(num,map.getOrDefault(num,0)+1);
        }

        return count;
    }
}
